Bulk Edit Help

Use option 1 to edit the list of extension changes to be made using nano.

Add a command ( + , * , - , ~ ) and the extension name
Use + for adding a git-sourced extension that uses `wfLoadExtension( 'ExtensionName' );` in LocalSetting.php
Use * for adding a git-sourced extension that uses `require_once "$IP/extensions/ExtensionName/ExtensionName.php";` in LocalSetting.php
Use - to remove an extension (works for both git-sourced and Composer-sourced extensions)
Use ~package:version:ExtensionName to add a Composer-sourced extension, e.g. ~mediawiki/maps:~14.0:Maps
	- package is the Packagist package name (e.g. mediawiki/maps)
	- version is the Composer version constraint (e.g. ~14.0)
	- ExtensionName must exactly match the directory the package installs
	  itself as under extensions/ (check the extension's own documentation)

See the extension documentation at https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Extension:ExtensionName
to know which command to use when adding an extension.

In Addition
Use updatedb to run the update script to update the database schema, needed after adding some extensions.

For example:

 +ContactPage
 +AddMessages
 -Poem
 *ConfirmAccount
 +Echo
 ~mediawiki/maps:~14.0:Maps
 updatedb

To exit Ctrl+X then Y and Enter to save.

Use option 2 to run the list of extension changes to be made.